{
  "_doc": "POS-1238's seed of the World's landed door law, byte for byte. World #444 (WLD-253, CORE-129 layer 1) merged to postmark-world main as b775f7975fe221ab2377d1260a22366a0033a500; the office suite's pinned world clone (test/clone-pins.json) predates it by 361 commits, and moving that pin is its own issue. So test/door-class.test.mjs lays these files over a synthetic world built from the pinned clone's tools: the five tools are tools/door-law.mjs and the four modules it imports (class-properties, mark-kind, admin-makers, and claim-instant, which mark-kind imports), loaded by the office's own worldToolModule exactly as production loads them; the seventeen records are the Keeping Works class chain door reads (postmark-node, mark, sited, thing and door, each with its makers; mark's entry, thing's entry: none, and door's into, lands_at and requires), with the three marks they nest under, read by the office's own law-ingest (deriveLaw) into the law snapshot. Fetched with gh api repos/postmark-town/postmark-world/contents/<path>?ref=<sha> (Accept: application/vnd.github.raw). Do not edit: re-seed from a newer World sha, and the test holds every file to its sha256 below.",
